 ## Overview
-Robust SIRT is an algebraic reconstruction technique that modifies the standard Simultaneous Iterative Reconstruction Technique (SIRT) to be resilient to outliers in projection data by employing a Student's t-distribution likelihood model [S1, unofficial]. It builds on [Forward Projection](18234-forward-projection.md) by enabling specific robust weighting within the ASTRA projector framework [S1, unofficial]. Unlike standard SIRT, which minimizes the L2-norm of residuals and is sensitive to noise spikes, Robust SIRT down-weights large residuals, making it suitable for data with impulsive noise or artifacts [S1, unofficial].
+Robust SIRT is an iterative reconstruction method that uses ASTRA's projector with a `student` flag enabled to apply robust weighting during updates [S1, unofficial]. It builds on [Forward Projection](18234-forward-projection.md) by leveraging subset processing for memory efficiency [S1, unofficial]. Unlike standard SIRT, it down-weights large residuals to handle impulsive noise or artifacts [S1, unofficial].
 
