 ## Background
-Robust SIRT is an extension of the Simultaneous Algebraic Reconstruction Technique (SIRT) [S2, unofficial]. SIRT was introduced by Andersen and Kak in 1984 [S2, unofficial]. The robust variant using Student's t-distribution is implemented in the ASTRA toolbox and utilized in frameworks like flexTOMO [S1, unofficial]. It is used in tomographic applications where data quality is compromised by noise or artifacts, such as in infrared radiance reconstruction from axisymmetric sprays [S2, unofficial].
+The method is implemented in the ASTRA toolbox and utilized in frameworks like flexTOMO [S1, unofficial]. It is applied in tomographic reconstruction where robust weighting is required [S1, unofficial]. The variants CAV and Cimmino are discussed in the context of axisymmetric spray tomography [S2, unofficial].
 
